 "reasoning": "Wikipedia names the site 'Oakmere hill fort', with coordinates 53.206022, -2.635518, a few metres from the stored point. The Atlas of Hillforts of Britain and Ireland (Universities of Oxford and Edinburgh; ArcGIS dataset record EN3192, lat 53.2056, lon -2.6363, scheduled monument 1013291) catalogues the same site as the hillfort 'Oakmere, Cheshire', an inland promontory fort also called Oakmere Camp. Historic England's scheduling title calls it 'Oakmere promontory fort'. A promontory fort is a type of hillfort, so that title is a narrower designation of the same monument, not a different name. The served 'Oakmere Hill Fort' names the right site; it differs from Wikipedia only in capitalisation."
